const SPOTS=[
 {id:"s1",p:"knudsen",title:"Knudsen Equation Wall — E = mc²",prod:"E = mc² sticker",story:"Sparko once found a giant equation glowing quietly on the wall of Knudsen.\nIt didn’t understand every symbol, but it liked the idea that something so small could hold so much energy.\nSo whenever Sparko feels tiny on a big campus, it comes back here to remember:\nsmall things can carry more than you think."},
 {id:"s2",p:"boelter",title:"Boelter Hall — LEGO Wall",prod:"LEGO Wall sticker",story:"Sparko discovered the LEGO wall one afternoon and immediately decided it was the perfect hiding place.\nOne colorful block became a chair.\nAnother became a table.\nA tiny gap became Sparko’s secret room.\nSince then, Sparko has believed that big things are often built from very small pieces.\nOne block, one idea, one little step at a time."},
 {id:"s3",p:"planetarium",title:"Math Sciences Planetarium",prod:"Planetarium sticker",story:"One night, Sparko slipped into the planetarium and looked up at a sky filled with stars.\nFor a moment, campus felt enormous.\nThen Sparko noticed that every star was just a tiny point of light.\nIt stayed there for a while, wondering how something so small could still be seen from so far away.\nMaybe you don’t have to be big to shine."},
 {id:"s4",p:"mathroof",title:"Math Sciences Rooftop — Cardioid Equation",prod:"Cardioid sticker",story:"On the rooftop of Math Sciences, Sparko found a curve shaped almost like a heart.\nIt followed the line carefully, step by step, until it looped all the way around.\nSparko liked that a complicated equation could create something so simple and familiar.\nNow, whenever life feels messy, Sparko remembers:\neven complicated things can still make a beautiful shape."}
];
